greeny@thelair.zynet.com (J. S. Greenfield) writes:

[...]
>As for FERPA, it applies to educational records, and it's not clear to me
>that it would apply to these kind of computer records.
[...]

The FERPA applies to any university records with personally
identifiable information about students. It is the law that stops
schools that take federal funds from posting grades with Social
Security Numbers or Names. It is also the law that requires schools
that take federal funds to ask if you, a student, want to be listed in
the University phone book.

Either:
   Student files on university computers are university records
      and thus covered by the FERPA.
Or
   They are not university records at all and thus are not covered
      by Sunshine/FOIA laws.

Either way, state FOIA can't require disclosure.

- Carl

